A||N||8||GT-maniac||Slalom Racing||||7||
Z||000000||GT-maniac||08-21-2001||03:34 AM||||Well our local fiero club just came back from a day of slalom racing. What a blast ! I definitely want to do this again. We turned in respectable times but didn't really have a chance at beating too many of the other cars. It's hard to beat run times of 200 + HP Miatas and corvettes when you've only got 140 HP fiero's. They were all beating our straightaway times. Best any of us could do was 7 seconds down the first straightaway and they were doing it in 5. That's ok though one of our guys is going to put in a supercharged 3800 next month and then we'll see what happens. Still going to be tough though I think as these Miata guys are pretty serious, over half of them were turbocharged. They were beating the vettes too. Funniest thing was seeing a guy go around in a new cobra, did all right though beat us by 4 seconds. All that straight line power again I guess. Also a camaro did a nice 360 at the first turn on one of his runs. Also saw a GTP go through the course, that thing looked huge but he did almost as well as the mustang.<BR>Our best times were about 4 - 5 seconds slower than even the vette with racing slicks on which was not too bad for cars which cost about 30000 less with street tires. I could tell the corvette club members which put on the race weren't too happy, especially with the miatas beating them. <P>I can post some pics if anybody wants to see them. They're taken with my cheap digital camera though so the quality is not the best.<P>Unfortunately I now have a broken shift select cable in my 4 speed from one too many fast down shifts so if anyone has one for sale..<p>[This message has been edited by GT-maniac (edited 08-21-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000001||ChadMan||08-21-2001||08:41 AM||||I assume "slalom racing" is what you fellas up North call "autocrossing," right?  It is a blast...I had so much fun losing, I can't imagine how much fun it will be if I ever win anything.<P>There was a guy with a Grand Prix GTP racing the day I was there and did surprisingly well.  Maybe wider IS better.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Sure, let's see your pics!<p>[This message has been edited by ChadMan (edited 08-21-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000002||GT-maniac||08-29-2001||04:05 PM||||Here's the link to the pics I promised.<BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=1768840&a=13660705&f=0" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=1768840&a=13660705&f=0</A> <P><p>[This message has been edited by GT-maniac (edited 08-29-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000003||thomas_l||08-29-2001||04:26 PM||||I did a real crowd-pleasing smoky doughnut (overdrove a fast "S" curve) in my 87 GT at the SCCA autocross weekend before last. The round of applause from the crowd was a hoot! Too bad my wife didn't show up with the camcorder in time to catch it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Eric||08-29-2001||07:27 PM||||Chadman, are you planning on coming out to another autocross this summer?  There's one on Sunday I'm thinking of going to.||||reg||1
